## Verification

No browser or `st.testing` tooling was available for a full click-through, so
the app was verified two ways:

1. **Live server smoke test** — launched `streamlit run streamlit_app.py
   --server.headless true` in the background and curled the base URL and all
   four page routes; server log showed no tracebacks.
2. **`streamlit.testing.v1.AppTest`** (the real check — a plain `curl` to a
   Streamlit page route only fetches the static SPA shell, it doesn't execute
   the page's Python server-side): ran every page headlessly and asserted
   `at.exception` is empty, then exercised the interactive paths:
   - Page 1: switched to "Enter manually", clicked "Reset to dataset default",
     changed a selectbox, changed a slider — no exceptions.
   - Page 3: changed a selectbox, changed a slider, clicked "Reset sliders",
     clicked "Use this what-if scenario" — no exceptions.

   This caught one real bug: `st.image(..., use_container_width=True)` isn't
   supported in Streamlit 1.39 (added later) — raised `TypeError` on Global
   Insights. Fixed by switching every `st.image` call to `use_column_width=True`
   (the 1.39-compatible equivalent); `st.pyplot`/`st.dataframe` do accept
   `use_container_width` in 1.39 and were left as-is.

No screenshots were captured this session (no headless-browser tool available
in this environment) — running `streamlit run streamlit_app.py` locally and
screenshotting each page is a trivial follow-up, noted for Phase 4 polish.

